@startuml

title PENA-Agent — Use Case Model

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #444444
  BackgroundColor #F5F5F5
}

skinparam usecase {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

actor User
actor Developer

rectangle "PENA-Agent" {

  usecase "Collect Articles" as UC1
  usecase "Filter Noise" as UC2
  usecase "Evaluate Source Quality" as UC3
  usecase "Summarize Content" as UC4
  usecase "Categorize Information" as UC5
  usecase "Generate Digest" as UC6
  usecase "Adapt to User Context" as UC7
  usecase "Capture Feedback" as UC8
  usecase "Generate Observability Reports" as UC9
  usecase "Refine Specifications" as UC10
  usecase "Evaluate AI Workflow Quality" as UC11

}

User --> UC1
User --> UC6
User --> UC7
User --> UC8

UC6 --> UC2 : <<includes>>
UC6 --> UC3 : <<includes>>
UC6 --> UC4 : <<includes>>
UC6 --> UC5 : <<includes>>
UC6 --> UC7 : <<includes>>

Developer --> UC9
Developer --> UC10
Developer --> UC11

note bottom of UC11
PENA-Agent is intentionally both:
- a user-facing system
- and an SDLC2 engineering laboratory
end note

@enduml
